# pnpm and Nub compatibility evidence

Document capability levels separately: parsing; producer detection; graph conversion; byte-preserving no-op; semantic incumbent rewrite; migration; frozen validation; package-manager frozen acceptance; installed-graph verification; runtime verification; transaction recovery.

Do not claim semantic rewrite support from parse-only coverage. Do not claim frozen compatibility because Mew validation passed. Do not claim installed-graph compatibility because a lock-only command passed. Do not claim Nub executable compatibility from pnpm-derived fixtures.

Nub evidence must distinguish: derived-format fixture validation; actual Nub-generated fixtures; actual Nub executable immutable or frozen conformance.

When working on Nub compatibility:

- fetch current Nub documentation from official sources;
- record the fetch date;
- record the documented lock format and compatibility behavior;
- record the Nub version or revision where available;
- use Nub behavior as a compatibility target;
- do not describe Mew as a port or implementation of Nub.
<!-- MEW-PNPM-NUB-EVIDENCE_END -->
